but I have a feeling that's a long way away.

I like the new town in Slash, it makes it a bit easier to consolidate
all your stuff and ID things (but only a bit). It also introduces a
lot of fatal temptations (Hmm, I really want that magic lamp but I'm
not prepared to pay for it). I also enjoy the new classes and races
(doppleganger, vampire, flame mage) although I think some of them
might need a little balancing. I also like the new starter kit for
wizards (my preferred class). Some of the interface tweaks are great
(ie "r." to read grafitti) as well.
Basically I just like the added variety and unexpectedness of slashem.
The way I see it, the more stuff you cram into a game the less
predictable it becomes.

